# T-997: Reverse functional dependency resolution (type-system-health-s841-followup)
# Verifies that a class with FD (src) → (dst) and injective: true parses and
# typechecks without error.
#
# The injective: true flag enables reverse-FD back-propagation at the type stage.
# This test verifies the class declaration (with determines, resolver, injective)
# is accepted by the type checker.
#
# NOTE: Runtime dispatch of user-defined class methods is not yet wired up.
# End-to-end reverse FD (call-site inference of src from known dst) is a future milestone.
[
  # Coercible class with FD: src determines dst (injective resolver)
  Coercible: [class [let Coercible src dst]
    [determines: [[[src] dst]]  resolver: CoercibleResolver  injective: True]
    coerce: [Fn@dst [src]]]

  # Prove the class declaration was accepted: return a simple value
  result: 42
]

---

%.result
=== out
Int(42)
